.TH SOROAUTH 1 "" "soroauth 9375847-dirty" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soroauth \- build, sign and inspect Soroban authorization entries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soroauth
.I command
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soroauth
builds, signs and inspects Soroban authorization entries: the values a
Soroban contract's require_auth call needs when the authorizing address is
not the transaction's source account.
.PP
Entries are passed and printed as base64 XDR, so the tool composes with
anything that produces or consumes that: an RPC client, jq, or another
invocation of soroauth.
.PP
Secrets are never accepted as flag values. The sign subcommand reads a seed
from a named environment variable instead, which keeps it out of shell
history, out of the process table, and out of any transcript of the session.
No subcommand prints a secret, including on the error paths.
.PP
Run
.B soroauth
.I command
.B \-h
for a command's own flags. With --json, a command prints a single JSON
object on stdout and, on failure, a JSON object with an "error" field.
