.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
print the usage text
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
success
.TP
.B 1
general error (internal or unclassified)
.TP
.B 2
usage error (invalid flags, missing required flags, malformed input)
.TP
.B 3
signing refused (no matching node, already signed, unsupported credentials)
.TP
.B 4
verification failed (signature mismatch, invalid expiration)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Configuration values are resolved in precedence order: command-line flag, then
environment variable, then configuration file, then built-in default.
.TP
.B SOROAUTH_CONFIG
path to the JSON configuration file (defaults to $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/soroauth/config.json or $HOME/.config/soroauth/config.json)
.TP
.B SOROAUTH_NETWORK
default network name or passphrase for \-\-network
.TP
.B SOROAUTH_RPC_URL
default RPC endpoint for \-\-rpc-url, used by \-\-valid-for and doctor
.TP
.B SOROAUTH_SECRET_ENV
default environment variable name for \-\-secret-env (holds a variable name, never a secret value)
.TP
.B SOROAUTH_FORMAT
default output format (text, json, ascii, or dot)
